(a) to provide for the registration, inspection of public and private burial -

(b) to prescribe the depth of graves and places of interment and the space to be reserved between them;

(c) to prescribe the mode of making and keepof burial and places of cremation;

(d) to prescribe the form in which the register of burials and cremations shall be kept at each licensed burial or place of cremation, and the particulars with regard to each burial and cremation which shall be entered in such register;

(e) to prescribe the form of licences and the of publication or service of orders made under this Act; _,·

(f) to prescribe the fees, if any, to be taken in any licensed public burial or place of cremation;

(g) generally to carry out the provisions of this Act in relation to all matters connected with the management, upkeep and good order of burial and places of cremation, due regard being had to the religious usages to the several classes of the comand may attach to the breach of any such rules a penalty on conviction before a magistrate not exceeding $500.

